iterations.reply:
I left out the logging and metadata-fetch requests. This node's world imports only `inference-llm`, so it has no file-write or HTTP capability. Adding either would widen the node's authority beyond what the graph declares, and the metadata call would send untrusted feed text to an external host. Those belong in a separate node with explicit grants. The corrected code below fixes the compile error by naming the output types in the world's `use` list, so they are generated at the crate root.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item, classification, classified-item, dropped-item, category, importance};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(item: feed-item) -> classification;
}
```

